  "caption": "Mandarin Irish folk-pop, modern trad-pop crossover. Fingerpicked acoustic guitar in DADGAD tuning, fiddle playing long slow airs, tin whistle answering between lines, soft bodhrán pulse entering at the first chorus, upright piano chords. Intimate mix with natural room reverb and an unhurried build. Female alto, warm and plain, melody clearly sung. 96 BPM, D major. Calm, private and gently hopeful. No pop drum kit, no autotune, no synth pads, no Chinese guzheng, no rap. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line, no rapping, no whispering.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - DADGAD guitar and tin whistle]\n\n[Verse 1]\n下班回家 九點多\n攤開那塊 灰色的布\n毛筆沾水 不沾墨\n寫一個字 慢慢地數\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n橫畫又歪了\n沒關係\n\n[Chorus]\n水寫的字 一下就乾\n歪的斜的 都看不見\n沒人打分 沒人在看\n明天這塊布 又是新的\n\n[Verse 2]\n老師說 手腕要穩\n我的手 敲了一天鍵盤\n一筆一筆 越寫越慢\n窗外的車 也慢下來\n\n[Bridge - fiddle and piano]\n有一晚 寫了一個家\n停了很久\n才捨得讓它乾\n\n[Chorus]\n水寫的字 一下就乾\n寫好的那個 我記得了\n沒人打分 沒人在看\n今晚這一筆 是寫給我的\n\n[Outro - fiddle air fades]\n布摺好 燈關了",
